WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
(Audience): Good Morning, John, it's Friday!

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.080
(Audience cheering)

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:15.980
(Upbeat music)

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.040
Would anybody like a breakfast burrito?

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.080
There's a thing here. I don't know what it-

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.330
Is it cheaper for bands?

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:22.460
[oh], it's outside is this the thing?

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.600
(door creaking)

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:24.820
Oh, it's outside.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.260
(Katherine): Well you got to follow the footsteps

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.000
(Hank): Is this The Thing?

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:27.900
(Man): No.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:28.680
(Hank): Ok.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.060
(Man): I don't think you can broadcast what The Thing is.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.140
It'll just be a reaction video to The Thing.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:33.880
Do you like this?

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.300
I like The Thing.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.260
Made in Constantinople, or was it Istanbul?

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.220
Ok, another door and now we're in another person's yard.

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:43.940
Here's another shed!

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Is the thing in her-oh, I think The Thing is in here.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:46.860
Is this The Thing?

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.440
Here lies The Thing.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:50.300
Ohhh.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.700
(wheezing laughter)

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.460
Ooooh.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:55.460
(All): Whoa!

00:00:55.960 --> 00:01:02.480
(All): What? Whoa! Oh No! Who-ho-ho What? Seriously?

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:04.760
(All): What is that?

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:05.620
(All): Ew, Eughhh

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:06.160
(Katherine): Is that real?

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.740
There aren't any informational placards, about it, at all.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.460
Well, it's here, so it's real.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:11.720
Right, it does exist.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.360
(Katherine) It's real. Yeah. I'm looking at The Thing.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.420
(door squeaking)

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.260
My curiousity is unsatisfied.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:16.830
Some things aren't meant to be known, like

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:17.840
for example

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.780
For example, I guess, The Thing.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:35.800
(Fast guitar playing)

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:39.180
(loud stomping echo)

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.720
We got a melted Hershey Bar.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:41.860
Just, like, make a little hole

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:42.780
Suck it all out!

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:43.700
Wanna try?

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.200
Nope!

00:01:44.200 --> 00:02:04.120
(Slow, calm music)

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:04.660
(music starts to pick up)

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:16.560
(faster, upbeat music)

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.260
We have regrets.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:18.700
(sigh)

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.600
It's been uphill for a long time. (exhausted)

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:27.600
(guitar music)

00:02:27.600 --> 00:03:09.640
(guitar and saxophone music)

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.880
Oh, last show is over!

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:14.680
There's a ladder here, I don't know where it goes, I'm gonna try to go up.

00:03:14.680 --> 00:03:19.760
(Crowd chattering in background)

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:20.760
I don't feel like risking it.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.960
Nope. Just cool lighting up here.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.280
It's not-not built for people with my disposition.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:26.420
This was really fun.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.200
So many great shows, so many great people.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:29.740
(sigh)

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:31.680
I really like our community.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:33.900
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

